# Snapshot fixture bodies are raw upstream bytes, verified on load by
# body_sha256 in each snapshot's manifest.json — see docs/snapshot-format.md,
# rule 3. A checkout that rewrites line endings changes those bytes, which
# fails the hash check and makes every check/route test depending on a
# snapshot fail — not because the fixture is wrong, but because the checkout
# edited it. This is exactly the class of drift core.autocrlf introduces on
# a default Windows git config, so these paths are pinned to the bytes as
# committed regardless of any user or global autocrlf setting.
checks/testdata/snapshots/**   -text
testdata/snapshots/**          -text
